WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
The Ganges plain, around
the 5th century BCE.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.750
Cities, trade and
kingdoms are growing fast.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.960
Priests pour offerings into a sacred fire.

4
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.760
Some rites include animal sacrifice.

5
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.760
Meanwhile, wandering seekers
leave home, beg for food,

6
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.770
meditate and debate.

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.710
The Buddha rejected the
priests' sacrifices.

8
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.470
So why did he still call
the best people brahmins?

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.730
In this mission, you'll meet
the rival teachers of his time,

10
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.070
from fatalists and
materialists to the Jains.

11
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.340
Then you'll read his sharpest
criticisms of the priests,

12
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.650
and weigh up whether he was
a reformer or a founder.

13
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: find out why he still
called the best people brahmins.
